# Haui.PCB C# / WPF Rules

## Layering

- **ViewModels** and **Processing** — all business and vision logic
- **Views** (`*.xaml.cs`) — UI events, `Dispatcher`, control updates only
- Never put segmentation, comparison, or file I/O in code-behind beyond delegating to ViewModel

## Services

Add abstractions under `Haui.PCB/Processing/{Domain}/` (Camera, Segmentation, Templates, …):

- `ICameraService`, `IPcbSegmentationService`, `ITemplateLibraryService`
- `ITemplateLibraryService`, `IRegionComparisonService`, `IPipelineDebugService`

Wire implementations in the window constructor (see `MainWindow.xaml.cs`).

## OpenCV / resources

```csharp
using var mat = new Mat();
// Dispose every Mat; caller disposes frames passed between windows
```

Convert to WPF with `BitmapSourceConverter.ToBitmapSource(mat)` then `.Freeze()`.

## C# style

- File-scoped namespaces theo folder: `namespace Haui.PCB.Processing.Camera;` (xem `GlobalUsings.cs`)
- `using var` for `IDisposable`
- `_camelCase` private fields; PascalCase public members
- Vietnamese comments OK for non-obvious vision logic
- No new NuGet packages without strong justification

## Async

Use `async`/`await` for camera refresh and long I/O; marshal UI updates via `Dispatcher`.
